WEBVTT

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.330
"Welcome"

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:40.040
Claudia.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.950
At least once in your life,
you should visit Japan.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:45.950
Japan?

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:49.080
Yeah. The samurai country.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:54.040
I wasn't there long, but I learned
many things while I was there.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:56.200
Samurai?

00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:01.990
Unbreakable, unyielding, men of pride.
Bravery is their way of life.

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:04.950
And the women who support them...

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:09.790
...are kind and graceful,
striving to be ideal women.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.290
I want to raise you as strong as a samurai...

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:19.160
...and as graceful as their women.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:24.450
I only wish you could live in a
world without the worry of Pillars.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:27.200
Father...

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.990
Enough being gloomy. I'll tell you some stories.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:34.450
About the days I soared
through the skies of Japan...

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:41.870
Ever since, I yearned for the
chance to visit this country, but...

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:45.660
Unbreakable, unyielding, men of pride...

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:48.790
Kind and graceful...

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:54.910
I don't want to doubt my father's stories,
but what's up with this base?

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.240
Found you! Claudy spotted!

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:00.790
Let's have a get-together!

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:38.200
Whew! Didn't think you'd be in the dojo!
I ran all over looking for you!

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:38.570
Episode 2: 
Umihotaru Sea Assault !

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.370
Is that <i>hakama</i> and katana yours?

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:48.290
Yeah. My father brought them back
from when he was stationed in Japan.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:52.910
Really?! Your father was in the military too?

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:59.370
He was an exceptional aviator.
Now, I'm following in his footsteps.

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:06.240
I see! Well, I'm glad to hear it!

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:11.990
It means your father loved Japan, right?
That makes me super happy!

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:13.830
Does it?

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:19.080
Of course! I feel like we'll
get along even better now!

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:25.660
And? Is this get-together supposed to help?

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:28.450
Didn't we party plenty last night?

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:32.950
That was different!
This time, it's just the Valkyrie Wing!

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:36.540
We're comrades that will
overcome Ragnarök together!

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:40.290
Getting along is funda-fricken-mental!

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:42.790
Is that how it is?

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:44.620
That's how it is!

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:48.240
All righty! Let's meet up at the cafeteria then!

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:53.370
I'll drag Azu along, so you go and fetch Sono!

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:59.490
Oh, sorry! I think Sono's around
back by the garden! See you soon!

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:21.200
Huh? Claudy!

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.990
What a lovely garden.

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:29.620
It is! There's so many growing now
thanks to everyone's help.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:32.040
You're up early today.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:35.990
Too much sleep is a soldier's worst enemy.

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:41.080
I got in the habit of waking up
early before I even knew it.

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:44.830
And I used to be a late riser too. Strange...

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:49.660
Did you sleep well after last night?

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:55.120
All that craziness hardly
facilitates a good night's sleep.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:58.120
You're right about that.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:02.580
The Shield Squadron trio made
for an interesting band.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:06.290
Having three vocalists is a bit much, right?

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:08.330
And the operator team's act?

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:11.290
It wasn't the best, but it had its moments.

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:14.080
I have high hopes for next time.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:16.160
The commander's dance...

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:17.660
No comment.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:19.160
That's harsh.

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:23.580
He'll get carried away if you encourage him.

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:26.160
Has our strange base shocked you?

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:32.290
I'd be lying if I said otherwise.
Is this what all of Japan is like?

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:37.870
Rest assured. This base is a special,
one-of-a-kind sort of place.

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:42.080
Well, I wouldn't really call that reassuring.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:50.450
Ugh... I'm so sleepy, my brain won't work.

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:53.080
Feeling the effects of the party?

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:56.910
Geniuses have their own problems.
Please be quiet--

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:59.370
Hey! I brought you some breakfast!

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:00.620
Damn you!

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:06.040
Huh? What? Oh! I took out
all the foods that you hate!

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:10.240
But it's important to eat everything,
so let's work on that!

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:14.200
Can we just not? Argh! Forget it!

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:17.370
So, about this get-together...

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:23.700
Yeah, that! Yesterday was a bit crazy,
but now we can sit down and talk!

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:27.040
We're a team! We're Valkyrie sisters!

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:30.120
We've gotta work together and "fire"!

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:31.740
Right, guys?!

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:33.120
--Yeah...
--Sure...

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:34.700
I can't hear you!

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:36.290
Yeah!

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:37.950
Mean it this time!

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:39.740
Yeah!

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:41.990
Are you always like this?

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:45.160
Of course! Turn that frown upside down!

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:47.580
Let's go! Introduction time!

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:49.450
That's our Miko!

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:51.450
The life of Tateyama!

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.450
She's our sunshine!

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:57.290
Yup! Happy is best! Happy is life!

00:07:57.290 --> 00:08:00.040
My name is Miyako Muguruma!

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:05.080
In my shiny, bright red Ki-44,
I go "boom" and "fire"!

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:05.080
Fire

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.620
Fire!

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:08.200
F-Fire...

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:10.290
Okay! Next up is Azu!

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:14.950
All that enthusiasm won't work on me.

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:19.580
I'm Azuzu Komagome.
As you can see, I'm a genius.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:22.370
I fly a modified He100.

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:23.990
Modified?

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:29.330
I swapped out the engine and armor
so it's just the way I want it.

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:33.490
Y-You modified a Hero Wing
that's a gift from god?

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:37.450
The only reason that's
possible is because "I" did it!

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:40.790
Still, since it's not exactly stable,

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:44.540
no one else will let me
tinker with their planes.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:48.330
It's her dream to work on
other people's Hero Wings.

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:52.450
You wanna help everyone's
odds of survival, right?

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:54.620
Th-That's not true!

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:58.290
M-My genius is made for much bigger things!

00:08:58.290 --> 00:08:59.990
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:05.620
I'm Sonoka Watarai, Valkyrie of the pink M.C.72.

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:09.790
Unlike Miko and Azu,
there's not much to say about me.

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:12.200
She's Japan's youngest ace!

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:14.490
She's our speed demon beauty!

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:17.160
Tateyama's swiftest angel!

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:19.660
They seem to think differently.

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:21.870
No comment.

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:24.160
Now then! At last...!

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:27.160
Yeah! Time for the star of the show!

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:30.290
--Yeah!
--Woohoo!

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:35.290
First impressions are really important.
Just remember that.

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:39.740
We're comrades that will
overcome Ragnarök together!

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:42.410
Comrades, huh?

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:45.490
Um, you don't really have to.

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:47.330
Sono, just chill.

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:49.330
--Ahem!
--Whoa!

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:54.080
I-I am Claudia Bruford!

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:54.990
The Gjally!

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:57.160
It's "Gjallarhorn."

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:03.450
Let's go, newbie!

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:04.910
Hurry, hurry!

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:06.660
We'll finish later!

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:11.990
As if I'd finish that!

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:15.160
Sigururi.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:19.330
Sigururi.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:23.120
We just blasted a Pillar yesterday!

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:26.160
That was just a stray one from the sea.

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:30.240
Besides, this one might not
be in our jurisdiction.

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:32.370
Azu, look!

00:10:32.370 --> 00:10:33.870
Whose area is that?

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:35.910
Ours, right?

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:38.040
See?! It's your fault again!

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:40.700
How is this my fault?!

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:43.450
Guys! Going out to scout?

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:46.910
You know it. We'll go and check things out.

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:50.120
Just sit back and wait for the good news.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:52.660
We'll go blast the hell out of it!

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:54.660
Be careful! Good luck!

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:57.910
Thanks. We're not gonna botch it.

00:10:57.910 --> 00:11:00.160
We'll be careful, so don't worry.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:02.950
Hey! Don't monopolize her!

00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:06.410
Miko! Can I get a reward when we come back?

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:09.740
Okay! I'll make you breakfast tomorrow!

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:11.490
Hell yeah! Let's go!

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:12.990
Woohoo!

00:11:12.990 --> 00:11:16.290
Better now? Let's get to the war room.

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:18.120
Right. Let's go!

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:19.580
Here's the image.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:22.370
Where is it?

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:24.540
Kisarazu Artificial Island.

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:30.240
It looks like a fixed-position type,
but analysis isn't complete yet.

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:35.200
Kisarazu Artificial Island. Umihotaru, huh?

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:37.910
Thank god I didn't get hammered.

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:39.540
Team lead, status?

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:42.790
Stayed up all night to fix 'em for you.

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:45.450
As usual, you run a tight ship.

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:48.910
I guess all my worrying came in handy.

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:50.290
What's it doing?

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:53.620
We're waiting to hear from recon.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:57.370
Being on water,
it shouldn't cause too much harm.

00:11:57.370 --> 00:12:01.990
Recon here! It's affecting
the civilians still in the area!

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:02.870
What?!

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:04.620
Th-That's awful!

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:06.490
Not good...

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:08.240
Hurry with the analysis!

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:11.540
Calculate how long they have to be rescued!

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:12.910
Yes, sir!

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:17.330
Commander! Give us permission to land!
We can save a few!

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:21.790
No, I won't allow it!
We don't know what the Pillar is doing!

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:23.290
But...!

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:25.620
What was that?!

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:27.540
Commander, the sea is--

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:32.830
Send out rescue!

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:35.660
Call for assistance from Yokosuka!

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:36.700
Roger!

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:37.910
Commander!

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:39.240
What's the status?

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:40.990
There you are.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:48.200
There's a barrier of water around the Pillar.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:53.410
It's surrounding Umihotaru and
neither cannons nor missiles penetrate it.

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:57.740
The recon crew was there
when the barrier went up.

00:12:57.740 --> 00:12:59.200
The recon crew?

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:03.120
We've gotta save everyone! Let us go out!

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:04.200
Denied.

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:05.620
Why?!

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:10.290
It's a fixed-position type
with a water barrier to top it off.

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:14.330
It's beyond reckless to go out
with no chance of winning.

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:17.870
I don't want my Valkyries dying for nothing.

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:22.950
There's more than just Valkyries!
No one should die, no matter who!

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:24.620
Miko...

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:31.990
I've calculated how long we have
to save the civilians and recon, but...

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:33.580
How long is it?

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:38.410
Being optimistic, just 3,600 seconds.

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:46.910
Ship cannons can't pierce its barrier
and planes will just be target practice.

00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:51.160
Unless we get inside the barrier, it's hopeless.

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:55.120
What's this?

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:57.290
That's the Tower of Wind.

00:13:57.290 --> 00:14:00.660
It's a tourist attraction near Umihotaru.

00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:03.370
Can we talk tourism another time?

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:04.950
That's it!

00:14:04.950 --> 00:14:06.870
Is the Aqua-Line flooded?

00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:07.910
It's not.

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:11.490
Nice! Way to keep us in the game, newbie!

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:13.240
You had an idea?

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:14.870
Yeah!

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:17.950
Man, I am such a genius!

00:14:17.950 --> 00:14:21.490
Shield Squadron, prepare to launch.
Be safe out there!

00:14:21.490 --> 00:14:26.580
Listen, you stooges! If you go and die,
at least spare the planes!

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:27.330
Hey!

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:31.790
Got it! He sure has weird ways
of showing his love.

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:34.370
Let's go keep 'em safe and sound.

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:36.790
Shield Squadron, takeoff!

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:47.240
909th Valkyrie Wing, ready for takeoff!

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:50.620
Sigrdrifa 909, takeoff!

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:52.290
Roger!

00:15:00.740 --> 00:15:02.830
Will this actually work?

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:06.370
Just do what I said and it can't go wrong!

00:15:06.370 --> 00:15:08.870
That really makes me worry.

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:11.200
It'll be fine, Sono!

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:14.700
After all, Claudy signed off on it too!

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:16.450
Through the tunnel?!

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:20.290
Yup! The Tower of Wind
right beside the Pillar...

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:23.740
...is the Aqua-Line's ventilation tunnel.

00:15:23.740 --> 00:15:29.240
And if the line isn't flooded, it means
the water barrier isn't underground!

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:32.370
I've never flown through a tunnel before!

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:36.120
Is there even a way out if we make it that far?

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:39.830
Wait... Surprisingly, this plan might work.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:43.700
If I may, I'd like to fly lead for it.

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:48.080
I had a feeling you would ask that.
I saw it coming.

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:51.660
Good. Then, Schwertleite flies lead.

00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:54.200
The three of you will back her up.

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:57.160
Now, as for the plan name...

00:15:57.160 --> 00:15:57.890
Me!

00:15:57.890 --> 00:15:59.450
Muguruma?

00:15:59.450 --> 00:16:01.290
Sneaky Eel Plan!

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:05.410
You're closing in on the target zone.

00:16:05.410 --> 00:16:08.660
We'll keep the enemy's attention away from you!

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:10.830
Head straight for the Aqua-Line!

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:12.370
Don't get hurt!

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:13.870
Got it!

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:16.910
The enemy's attack range is ten kilometers.

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:18.580
Stay out of range!

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.370
Roger!

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:27.830
Break!

00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:30.540
Nice! Just as planned!

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:34.790
There! It's the Aqua-Line entrance!

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:36.120
Good!

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:39.160
Now then, Sneaky Eel Plan, commence!

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:40.990
Why couldn't we pick a better--

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:43.040
In we go!

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:49.330
Will it take us to the Tower of Wind?

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:51.450
I really hope so.

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:54.410
Pillar dead ahead!

00:16:56.830 --> 00:16:58.620
Stationary Pillars?!

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:01.990
Leave it to me! Sondergerät!

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:08.290
There's more from behind?!

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:10.910
Just hang in there! Do that and we win!

00:17:10.910 --> 00:17:12.470
"Tower of Wind (Kawasaki Artificial Island) Marker"
"57m Below Sea"

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:13.620
I see it!

00:17:13.620 --> 00:17:15.450
Let's go, guys!

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:18.910
Punch through!

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:22.950
Hell yeah! It's right there!

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:24.990
The plan worked!

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:27.040
Hurry! Before it attacks!

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:28.870
Right!

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:32.200
The first hit goes to me!

00:17:33.410 --> 00:17:34.950
A water wall?!

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:38.870
And here we finally got inside!

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:40.290
The barrier!

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:42.290
Control, you see this?

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:44.290
Yeah, we see it.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:46.290
Send rescue to Umihotaru!

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:47.080
Roger!

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:51.330
Whew! Looks like the girls made it inside!

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:53.580
Claudy, look! The top!

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:56.700
All right, it's do or die! Let's go!

00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:58.660
Aye aye, sir!

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:03.620
We're hitting the Pillar from above.
You two, keep it busy down below.

00:18:03.620 --> 00:18:04.790
Roger!

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:07.790
All right! Let's blow it to smithereens!

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:10.660
Azu, you sounded just like Miko now.

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:13.790
That's the worst thing I've ever heard.

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:19.450
The Vandrande!

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:20.950
Here goes!

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:25.200
Hero Cannon, fire!

00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:30.830
Claudy! Miko!

00:18:32.490 --> 00:18:35.290
We're good! No problems here!

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:36.870
Hunky-dory!

00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:38.580
Don't scare us like that!

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:40.370
You did it!

00:18:41.540 --> 00:18:43.450
Steam?

00:18:49.830 --> 00:18:51.790
Miyako, evade!

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:54.870
Whoa, whoa!

00:18:54.870 --> 00:18:56.740
That flame was...

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:02.370
Boogy cone!

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:06.290
It's "buccal cone,"
but there's no time to argue!

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:13.040
Let's try again!

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:14.410
Why?!

00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:16.450
Does the heat block weapons?

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:18.330
Claudy, what now?!

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:19.870
We can't win like this.

00:19:19.870 --> 00:19:21.910
No, we can!

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:24.160
Sono, did you pack it?

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:26.870
Oh! Yeah, I sure did!

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:30.410
Good! Then its heat won't be a problem!

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:32.330
Unload everything you've got!

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:34.160
Bombs away!

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:40.240
Was that coolant?!

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:45.040
For in case the place caught fire.
I'm sure glad we brought it!

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:45.990
Miko!

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:47.160
Roger!

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:51.990
My last big boom! Fire!

00:19:53.620 --> 00:19:56.450
There it is! Claude, it's all you!

00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:04.240
My name is Claudia Bruford!

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:08.830
I am Valkyrie Schwertleite,
and I fly a Gladiator!

00:20:11.450 --> 00:20:14.160
It's a pleasure to work with you!

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:47.790
Claudy!

00:20:47.790 --> 00:20:49.370
Whoa...

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:52.200
We did it! Victory!

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:55.370
We sure did. That was some good teamwork.

00:20:55.370 --> 00:21:00.080
Well? Do you think you'll get along
with everyone at the base?

00:21:00.080 --> 00:21:02.120
I wasn't sure at first.

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:06.620
Honestly, I thought I'd been sent
to a base full of nutcases.

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:13.330
But, had I been working alone,
there would've been no victory today.

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:19.410
Your service records are a mishmash,
and your planes as quirky as can be, but...

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:22.080
But, we're strong!

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:25.330
If we all want and hope for the same thing,

00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:29.370
I know we'll all get along just fine!

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:32.540
Yeah. I think you're right.

00:21:35.370 --> 00:21:39.950
Hey, I hope you're not letting
that idiot influence you.

00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:41.870
Don't let her.

00:21:41.870 --> 00:21:45.620
Because you're afraid
you'll start liking her more?

00:21:45.620 --> 00:21:47.410
Hey now!

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:52.580
Azuzu.

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:54.160
Sonoka.

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:55.490
Miyako.

00:21:55.490 --> 00:21:58.080
I have lots to learn, but...

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:01.040
...let's get along!

00:23:29.540 --> 00:23:33.080
Look at that wonderful smile you have now.

00:23:33.080 --> 00:23:36.660
You've been blessed with wonderful comrades.

00:23:36.660 --> 00:23:42.830
I'm glad you're having fun, Claudia...
My cute daughter.

00:23:42.830 --> 00:23:46.120
Get along with your new friends.

00:23:46.120 --> 00:23:49.660
At least, until twilight comes.

00:23:57.540 --> 00:23:58.950
What a welcome party!

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:00.660
Our secret practice paid off!

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:02.040
The power of teamwork!

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:04.830
Hell yeah! We're the Shield Squadron!

00:24:04.830 --> 00:24:05.870
Teamwork makes...

00:24:05.870 --> 00:24:06.830
...the dream work!

00:24:06.830 --> 00:24:07.950
But the truth is,

00:24:07.950 --> 00:24:10.080
I'm the best singer!

00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:12.080
Episode 3: 
Disaster Recovery Assessment !

00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:12.080
Wh-What?!
